      "writtenOn": "2022-06-03T20:24:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e So caching a positive result and then never checking again may cause an issue if charger_ready is set, then the battery is drained or unplugged, and the CPU is turned off, and then the battery is charged again, but the CPU is never turned on again.\n\nYes, this is according to legacy implementation CL:753294. During off time due to low power state user must press power button for the system to power on automatically as soon as battery power becomes acceptable, otherwise system will remain off and battery will continue charging.",
      "parentUuid": "c9eedecd_00ffb335",
      "revId": "4ccc2e6d8f06ebda354a9bc2c220636888ba104e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
